# creator5-custom-firmware -- TEST configuration
#
#     cp test.env.example test.env
#
# Nothing in this file ever reaches a printer. It configures the replica --
# the printer's real rootfs under qemu-mipsel -- and nothing else. Build
# inputs and anything that ships live in config.env.

# ---- the replica's /usr/prog and /usr/data ---------------------------------
# REQUIRED for every test that runs inside the replica. It is the factory
# image -- the printer's real /usr/prog and /usr/data, giving the replica the
# genuine klipper daemons, nginx, python3, checkEboard, moonraker and, most
# usefully, the printer's own OpenSSL 1.0.2d, so package decryption is
# verified against the real implementation. There are no stubs: if this is
# missing the replica refuses to run rather than test against mocks.
#
# One image serves both models. Either take one off your own machine
#
#     ssh root@printer 'tar -cf - /usr/prog' > prog.tar
#
# or use the published factory image
# (md5 d2fdc0e1deb17c41cbb6016d55ab3031):
#
#     https://github.com/ghzserg/FF/releases/download/R/Creator5Pro-factory.tar.xz
PROG_DUMP="$HOME/Desktop/Creator5Pro-factory.tar.xz"

# Real partition sizes, from the `df -h` block of the stage-0 probe report.
# Until these are set the replica's prog/data partitions are unbounded, so an
# install that runs the machine out of space would pass here and fail there.
PROG_MB=""
DATA_MB=""

# ---- a prebuilt replica image ----------------------------------------------
# Skips the local unpack entirely (~1m35s -> ~15s). Built by
# test/build-printer-image.sh; it carries proprietary FlashForge firmware.
#   PRINTER_IMAGE=monstrofil/creator5-printer:pro
PRINTER_IMAGE=""
